WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Tom: I'm with Simon Willison, zeppelin expert.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.000
Simon: Hello!

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.680
Tom: Simon, tell them something they don't know.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.480
Simon: So..

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.300
In 1910 the airship America

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.820
made the first ever attempt at a cross Atlantic crossing.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.680
And, on the way into the airship one of the engineers scooped up a stray cat,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.780
who'd been living in the hangar.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.260
The cat, they,

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.360
they christened the cat Kiddo, put him on the airship.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.000
Said: "This will be great, we'll take him along, he can be the ship's mascot."

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.440
Kiddo was not keen on this idea at all,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.460
kicked up a real stink,

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.740
and so once they got out of the Atlantic they transmitted the first ever radio message from an aircraft,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.360
and the message was: "Roy, come and fetch this goddamn cat.""

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.520
So, they sent a life boat out to fetch the cat.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.720
The cat was put in a bag, lowered down to a boat, really jumpy water,

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.920
the cat was furious, the waves were too choppy,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.900
they couldn't rescue him.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.680
They ended up having to hoist him back on board.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.820
"So, okay, we'll take him with."

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.120
The cat then settled down,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.720
obviously deciding the airship was a lot better than the bag.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.020
And, you know, it settled into the flight.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.100
They quickly discovered that he was the perfect companion,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.600
because cats are better than barometers:

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.440
the cat would get grumpy before they hit bad weather,

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.560
way before any of their instruments could detect it.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.200
That was all fine, but they were trying to cross the Atlantic.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.300
33 hours in, the airship broke,--

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.640
possibly because of sand that they picked up earlier--

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.160
they couldn't steer it, they found themselves adrift.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.740
They eventually spotted a Royal Mail ship out at sea,

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.920
managed to signal SOS to them,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.620
got rescued by it.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.860
And I think they made the first ever aerial SOS call as well.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.540
And they were rescued, along with the cat.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.340
The airship floated off and was never seen again.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.160
The Royal Mail ship went back to New York,

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:44.020
where Kiddo was put on display in the window of a fancy department store with a diamond necklace on

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.940
as a celebrity cat,

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.220
and he really did live the rest of his life out on the farm.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.700
Tom: Simon, thank you very much! That is something you might not have known.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:54.740
Simon: Thank you!

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.700
[Closed captions by MM. Translating these subtitles? Add your name here!]

